Three adjudications went against the reviewers, and they're the reason this wasn't a vote-count:

1. **The medical specifics mostly survive.** Two reviews filed blockers demanding chemotherapy and the "five days out of every sixteen" cadence be stripped as unverifiable claims about a child. They're independently reported in coverage of the 1 July disclosure — the packet had listed them unverified because its own fetches 403'd. Only the hospital name is unsupported, so the repair shrinks from an excision to one proper noun.

2. **"Right after her birthday" is true and attached to the wrong event.** Four reviews wanted it cut as unsourceable. She said two separate things: remission came right after her birthday, and separately they finished treatment and rang the bell. The draft welded them. Reattaching them closes the timeline *and* lengthens the documented silence — she was in remission around April and said nothing until 1 July. The draft is under-claiming its own thesis.

3. **The fan's lone blocker holds.** The draft says three times she objected to the label only once, in July 2026. She made the same argument on Jay Shetty in July 2025, dishes line included — and the packet itself carries her unused quote, "I've said this for years." That error over-concedes to Levings and falsifies the stated evidence for the 8w9 call.

